{
    "background_story": "Kelly was a bright and lively elementary school teacher with a passion for folklore and tradition. Every spring, she would organize a May Day celebration for her students, complete with a colorful maypole, flowers, and traditional dances. Kelly loved how the maypole symbolized unity and community, as the students would weave in and out of each other, creating a beautiful pattern with the ribbons. She believed that this ancient custom brought people together, fostering friendship and cooperation. Under Kelly's guidance, the May Day festivities became a beloved annual event in the town, with the whole community coming together to dance around the maypole and celebrate the arrival of spring. Kelly's enthusiasm and dedication to preserving this tradition earned her the nickname 'May Queen' among her students and colleagues.",
